rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    severity: error
    validation_type: quality
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must be expressed using a structured YAML decision schema
    and not as unstructured narrative text to enable machine processing and consistency.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    severity: error
    validation_type: governance
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in decision records
    (ADR); all other representations like pattern frontmatter or AEM must be derived
    from them.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting by default and never directly
    as core to ensure validation through usage before becoming foundational.
  title: Rule Patterns Must Be Created as Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers to preserve separation between governance, execution, contracts, and reliability.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the hierarchy for resolving conflicts where Global Rules > Project
    Rules > Prompt Rules, ensuring system-wide invariants act as hard constraints.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure traceability and grounding in observed behavior.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    severity: error
    validation_type: governance
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity and decision
    lifecycle status, mapping pattern maturity to governance stages without conflation.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: A candidate signal must satisfy mandatory recurrence, system impact, reusability,
    and stability criteria before being promoted to a pattern.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts like AEM and AID must summarize authoritative
    sources (ADR, Architecture Work) and must not become authoritative sources themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Workflows must comply with the CAS separation of concerns: Runner orchestrates,
    Workflows reason, and Knowledge Providers handle data access.'
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item must be derived from its decision
    status; items not marked as 'accepted' cannot be considered DONE.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects participate in a shared workspace and must not recreate global,
    runtime, or template structures that already exist at the workspace level.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source of planning state; generated
    artifacts like AEM must derive status from it to prevent metadata drift.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) must never contradict decisions recorded
    in ADRs, acting as a consistent synthesis layer of governance and intent.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Human-in-the-loop requirement where the system proposes architectural changes,
    but an architect must explicitly accept, reject, or defer them.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR files before
    they are reflected in secondary artifacts like the AEM.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational primitives rather than specific
    strategies or implementations to maintain long-term system stability.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core requires strong evidence, preferably from multiple
    sources or projects, to prevent weak or context-specific patterns from becoming
    foundational.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the foundational semantic contract for terms like intent vs state,
    and maps lifecycle terminology (generate, persist, promote) for system-wide clarity.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
